course: dictionary
lesson: 2421
title: Baby swans
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cygnet is a young swan, so a cygnet is a baby swan. When you meet this word in a text, look at the words around it for clues. «On the canal a swan rears up at Sam's dog, its wings booming like a door slamming; Sam's dad says a swan guarding cygnets (baby swans) can hurt a small dog badly.» The brackets give the meaning straight away: cygnets are baby swans.
explain: Context can also tell you what a swan does. It rears up, its wings boom, and it guards its young. Sam's dad warns that the swan can hurt a small dog. So the swan is protecting its cygnets, and it may be dangerous when it does.
explain: Cygnets do not look like adult swans. In nature lessons they are grey or brown and fluffy, and they often ride on their parents' backs. In the story «The Ugly Duckling», a grey, clumsy bird turns out to be a cygnet that grows into a beautiful white swan.
fact: A cygnet is a young swan.
fact: «Cygnets» means baby swans.
fact: Cygnets are grey or brown and fluffy when they are young.
fact: Family words: a cob is a male swan, and a pen is a female swan.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «The young swans followed their mother across the pond» still makes sense, so young swan is the right meaning.
exercise: «The cygnets followed their mother across the pond in a line.» What is a cygnet? | A male swan | A kind of fish | An old duck | *A young swan
exercise: In «The Ugly Duckling», the grey bird grows up into what? | A small owl | *A beautiful white swan | A brown hen | A grey goose
exercise: Which word is the family word for a male swan? | *Cob | Pen | Cygnet | Duckling
test: Ella says a cygnet is a little duck. What is the correct meaning of cygnet? | A grown-up swan | *A young swan | A baby duck | A baby goose
test: Which word means a female swan? | Cygnet | *Pen | Duckling | Cob
exam: Sam's dad warns that a swan guarding «cygnets» can hurt a small dog. What are cygnets? | *Baby swans | Baby ducks | Pet dogs | Fish eggs
